#![enable(implicit_some)]
// A synthetic parametric hull, generated for testing the hydrostatics
// pipeline. It is NOT a real design and is NOT taken from any published
// offset table: every number here comes from a smooth parametric form, and
// the coefficients land at Cb ~ 0.48, Cp ~ 0.62 -- fuller than a real cruising
// yacht, which sits nearer Cb 0.40.
//
// It exists because the analytic test shapes (barge, half-cylinder) exercise
// exactness but not fairness: this one has rocker, a fine bow, a broad
// transom, flare above the waterline and a section shape that varies along the
// length, which is what shakes out lofting and clipping bugs.
//
// Principal dimensions: Lwl 10.80 m, Bwl 3.40 m, canoe-body draft 0.62 m.
// No appendages: the schema has no place for them yet, so the mass properties
// describe a bare canoe body and the boat is correspondingly tender.
//
// Frame: x forward from the aft perpendicular, y half-breadth, z up from the
// baseline. All units SI.
